        "original_id": "644f2c66-72a4-592d-b06c-b9288393f4b9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, Roger Taylor, Taylor Hawkins, Lisa Carver\n- Music Groups: Sugarland, Soul Miner's Daughter, Jennifer Nettles Band, Foo Fighters, Queen\n- Songs: \"Everyday America\"\n- Places: Atlanta\n- Organizations: Planet Rock\n- Roles: lead singer, drummer\n\nFacts:\n- Before Sugarland was formed, Jennifer Nettles fronted the Atlanta-based bands Soul Miner's Daughter and Jennifer Nettles Band.\n- In 2005, Planet Rock listeners voted Roger Taylor the eighth-greatest drummer in classic rock history.\n- Roger Taylor was praised by Foo Fighters drummer Taylor Hawkins as one of the most influential rock drummers of the 1970s and 1980s.\n- Jennifer Nettles is best known as the lead singer of the duo Sugarland alongside Kristian Bush.\n- The song \"Everyday America\" was written by Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, and Lisa Carver.",
